akis (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Gus Bilirakis, a well-established Republican incumbent, is seeking re-election in a Tampa-area district with a Republican partisan lean of about seven points. He has raised roughly $1.6 million and holds a large cash advantage, while Democratic nominee Kimberly Overman enters the general with minimal funds. Expert forecasters overwhelmingly rate the race Safe or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a one-in-ten chance.\n\nThere are some signs of Democratic interest: the House campaign arm added the district to its target list, and a June poll sponsored by a Democratic firm showed a somewhat competitive landscape. Still, with no independent general-election polling, weak Democratic fundraising, and Bilirakis touting bipartisan legislative wins, the fundamentals point to a comfortable but not entirely risk-free Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0813, "margin": -8.73}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -9.5}]}